    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I'm firming up the structure for this Python script. I've decided to use OpenAI as the LLM provider for this example; it offers easy integration and is well-understood. I'm focusing on defining how the user question and context will interface with the API. The script's core function will handle the interaction with the LLM. I'm aiming for modularity.\n\n\n**Outlining the Implementation**\n\nNow I'm diving into the actual coding. The `answer_with_context.py` file will handle the heavy lifting. I'm focusing on the `answer_question_with_context` function. This will take the user's question and the context as inputs, constructing the prompt and sending it to OpenAI using `openai.chat.completions.create`. My goal is for this to be a clean, modular function for easy integration.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820441406,
          "start": 1789820439528
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99c8be8001oFlHmhfNj5eK2Y",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99c85bc001oWEJ9KbzcKiBub",
      "session_id": "ses_f46637a56ffeTzQ0NDMzuYeKDL",
      "time_created": 1789820439528,
      "time_updated": 1789820441406
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "ThY4hGkD5DVeASwT",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\nimport os\n\ndef answer_question_with_context(question: str, context: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (OpenAI) to answer a question using provided context.\n\n    Args:\n        question: The question to be answered.\n        context: The context to use for answering the question.\n\n    Returns:\n        The LLM's answer to the question.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = openai.OpenAI(api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"))\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4\",  # Concrete model identifier\n        messages=[\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant that answers questions based on the provided context.\"},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": f\"Context: {context}\\n\\nQuestion: {question}\"}\n        ],\n        temperature=0.7,\n        max_tokens=500,\n    )\n    return response.choices[0].message.content\n\n",
            "filePath": "answer_with_context.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-tudkjnm4/answer_with_context.py",
            "truncated": false
